{"step_index":194,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T19:30:52Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\n\"We are adding a 'Collision Avoidance Maneuver (CAM) Planner' to our Live Tracking tab. In real operations, avoidance maneuvers are very small thrusts, typically applied along the track of the orbit, to maximize distance from a potential conjunction. Satellites frequently use these delta-v burns for station-keeping and collision avoidance.\n\nPlease update index.html, app.js, and the Tailwind CSS with these exact features:\n\nCAM Drawer UI: Add a hidden right-side slide-out drawer (using a glassmorphism style: bg-black/80, backdrop-blur-lg, right-aligned). Add a close button.\n\nTrigger Mechanism: Update the 'Live Tracking' table so that clicking any row with a 'CRITICAL' risk badge opens the CAM Drawer and populates it with the selected objects' names.\n\nThrust Controls (Delta-v): Inside the drawer, build an interactive slider labeled 'In-Track Delta-v (m/s)' ranging from 0.0 to 2.0 m/s with a step of 0.1. Display the current slider value in a glowing text span next to the label.\n\nDynamic Simulation Chart: Below the slider, create a visual bar chart or progress bar titled 'Predicted Miss Distance'. Write vanilla JavaScript to simulate the maneuver: as the user drags the slider, multiply the Delta-v value by a mock expansion factor (e.g., 50 km per 0.1 m/s) and add it to the original miss distance. Update the visual bar and a 'New Miss Distance (km)' text metric in real-time.\n\nSafe Orbit Indicator: If the newly calculated miss distance exceeds 50 km, change the simulated risk badge inside the drawer from 'CRITICAL' (Red) to 'SAFE' (Green).\n\nAction: Write the updated HTML, JS, and CSS. Once running, use your embedded browser to click a CRITICAL row, drag the Delta-v slider to 1.5 m/s, and take a screenshot of the open drawer showing the updated SAFE miss distance.\"\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-24T01:00:52+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
