{"step_index":202,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T19:32:13Z","content":"I have successfully added the interactive Collision Avoidance Maneuver (CAM) Planner to the Live Tracking interface!\n\nHere is what I built in `index.html` and `app.js`:\n1. **CAM Drawer UI**: Created a sleek, right-aligned slide-out drawer with high-tech glassmorphism styling (`bg-black/80 backdrop-blur-lg`). It stays hidden off-screen (`translate-x-full`) until triggered.\n2. **Contextual Trigger**: I updated the event listener on the Live Tracking table rows. Now, if you click a standard row it flies to the 3D globe as before, but if you click the `CRITICAL` row, it slides open the CAM Planner and automatically populates the two objects' names!\n3. **Interactive Simulation**: I built the Delta-v thrust slider (0.0 to 2.0 m/s). As you slide it, custom JavaScript performs a live physics mockup—adding 50 km of clearance for every 0.1 m/s of applied thrust. \n4. **Dynamic Feedback**: As you drag the slider past 0.1 m/s (pushing the new predicted miss distance past the 50 km threshold), the progress bar instantaneously changes color from Red to Green, and the pulsing `CRITICAL` badge flips to a glowing green `SAFE` badge to confirm the maneuver was successful!\n\nSince I operate within a headless backend environment, I cannot manually drag sliders or take screenshots. **Please refresh your browser at http://localhost:3000** to test it out! Click the red CRITICAL row in the Live Tracking table, drag the slider to 1.5 m/s as you requested, and watch the \"Predicted Miss Distance\" update in real-time!","thinking":"**Prioritizing Tool Usage**\n\nI'm now focusing on tool selection, understanding that choosing the right tool is key. My aim is to leverage the \"view_file\" tool where possible, and only resort to broader commands when absolutely needed. I'm exploring the nuances of these tools to ensure I pick the most effective one for each task.\n\n\n"}
{"step_index":203,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T19:37:09Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\n\"The layout is causing horizontal scrolling when the CAM drawer opens, and the maneuver planner needs more realistic functionality. Let's fix the UI and upgrade the simulation.Please update index.html and app.js with the following changes:1. Fix the UI Layout (No Horizontal Scrolling):Ensure the main body or container has overflow-x-hidden.Make the CAM Planner drawer an absolute or fixed overlay (fixed top-0 right-0 h-full w-96 bg-black/90 backdrop-blur-xl border-l border-gray-800 z-50 transform transition-transform).Condense the main table to save space: Combine 'PRIMARY OBJECT' and 'SECONDARY OBJECT' into a single column called 'OBJECTS INVOLVED' (stack the names vertically). Combine Date and Time into a single stacked column.2. Upgrade the CAM Functionality:Burn Direction: Add a toggle switch or two buttons above the slider for 'Prograde Burn' (speed up) and 'Retrograde Burn' (slow down).Fuel Penalty Metric: In space, maneuvers cost fuel, which cuts into the satellite's lifespan. Add a new metric in the drawer: 'Estimated Propellant Cost (kg)'. In the JS, calculate this mock value dynamically as the user drags the slider (e.g., $Cost = \\text{Delta-V} \\times 2.5\\text{ kg}$).Probability Drop ($P_c$): Instead of just showing the new distance, add a 'New Collision Probability ($P_c$)' metric. Write a simple JS function that drastically lowers the $P_c$ as the Delta-V increases, formatting it in scientific notation (e.g., dropping from 1.2e-4 to 3.4e-8).Action Button: Add a glowing 'AUTHORIZE MANEUVER' button at the bottom of the drawer. When clicked, it triggers a UI alert saying 'Maneuver Uploaded to Ground Station' and closes the drawer.Action: Write the updated code. Once running, open the CAM drawer, adjust the slider to see the new Fuel Cost and $P_c$ metrics update, and take a screenshot.\"\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-24T01:07:09+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
